# Post-change test + release gate

After completing any **`/NF`**, **`/NB`**, or other **substantive code change** (not question-only or review-only turns):

1. **Always run `/testrelease`** — follow `.cursor/skills/test-release/SKILL.md` (context validate → Playwright batch suites → `pnpm test:build`).
2. If any step fails, **fix the errors and re-run `/testrelease` until it passes**.
3. After a **successful `/testrelease`**, **always run `/buildrelease`** — follow `.cursor/skills/build-release/SKILL.md` (`pnpm build:release`).
4. When done, **tell the user the exact batch/release that was built** (e.g. `v26.07.16b4`) and the installer path under `apps/desktop/release/` so they can QA.
5. Do not ask the user to test-release or build-release manually when you can run them yourself.

The Cursor **stop hook** (`.cursor/hooks.json`) still runs compile checks after agent turns. Treat hook failures as required fixes. That hook does **not** replace `/testrelease` or `/buildrelease`.

Skip this full gate only when the turn was read-only (no edits to `apps/`, `packages/`, or build scripts) or the PM explicitly waives packaging for docs-only work.
